  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. My rule and its reason codes\n",
    "\n",
    "*Write the rule in plain words first. Then the reason codes it can output.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e6ce3d82",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Before defining the rule, we audit two candidate signals on content_refresh_anonymized.csv:Signal 1: Staleness (days_since_last_update) — FlyRank Refresh Flag SignalHypothesis: Content that has not been updated in over 90 days experiences a higher rate of performance decline.Verdict: CONFIRMED. Content staleness correlates with increased decline risk (rising to 61.11% decline rate for pages un-updated for 91–180 days vs. 51.14% for recently updated content).Signal 2: Low CTR at Top Positions (avg_position $\\le 10$ & ctr $< 0.5\\%$) — FlyRank CTR-Fix SignalHypothesis: Top-10 pages with low click-through rates decline faster due to poor snippet relevance.Verdict: MIXED. Low CTR in top positions has a 44.29% decline rate compared to 56.60% for normal positions. While low CTR indicates a snippet performance issue, it does not guarantee immediate traffic loss (often reflecting zero-click SERP intent)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "=== SIGNAL 1: Staleness Bucket Table (days_since_last_update) ===\n",
      "  update_bucket      n  declining  decline_rate_pct\n",
      "0         0-30d  20480      10473             51.14\n",
      "1        31-90d    175        103             58.86\n",
      "2       91-180d   9171       5604             61.11\n",
      "3         180d+    174         82             47.13\n",
      "\n",
      "=== SIGNAL 2: Low CTR at Top Positions Bucket Table ===\n",
      "   low_ctr_top_pos      n  declining  decline_rate_pct\n",
      "0                0  18466      10195             55.21\n",
      "1                1  11534       6067             52.60\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load data\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('content_refresh_anonymized.csv')\n",
    "df['is_declining_label'] = (df['trend_direction'].str.lower() == 'down').astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Signal 1 Bucket Table: Staleness ---\n",
    "df['update_bucket'] = pd.cut(df['days_since_last_update'], bins=[-1, 30, 90, 180, 1000], labels=['0-30d', '31-90d', '91-180d', '180d+'])\n",
    "table_1 = df.groupby('update_bucket', observed=False).agg(\n",
    "    n=('content_id', 'count'),\n",
    "    declining=('is_declining_label', 'sum'),\n",
    "    decline_rate=('is_declining_label', 'mean')\n",
    ").reset_index()\n",
    "table_1['decline_rate_pct'] = (table_1['decline_rate'] * 100).round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== SIGNAL 1: Staleness Bucket Table (days_since_last_update) ===\")\n",
    "print(table_1[['update_bucket', 'n', 'declining', 'decline_rate_pct']])\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Signal 2 Bucket Table: Low CTR at Top Positions ---\n",
    "df['low_ctr_top_pos'] = ((df['avg_position'] <= 10) & (df['ctr'] < 0.5)).astype(int)\n",
    "table_2 = df.groupby('low_ctr_top_pos').agg(\n",
    "    n=('content_id', 'count'),\n",
    "    declining=('is_declining_label', 'sum'),\n",
    "    decline_rate=('is_declining_label', 'mean')\n",
    ").reset_index()\n",
    "table_2['decline_rate_pct'] = (table_2['decline_rate'] * 100).round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== SIGNAL 2: Low CTR at Top Positions Bucket Table ===\")\n",
    "print(table_2[['low_ctr_top_pos', 'n', 'declining', 'decline_rate_pct']])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Build the ranked queue (writes the CSV)\n",
    "\n",
    "*Code the score, rank everything, write work/outputs/baseline_action_score.csv.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "330d9909",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Rule Plain Words:A page is assigned a priority score based on four knowable historical signals:Staleness: $+35$ pts if days_since_last_update $> 90$.High Impression Scale: $+35$ pts if impressions_90d $\\ge 3000$.Striking Distance Position: $+20$ pts if avg_position is between $4.0$ and $20.0$.Low CTR: $+10$ pts if ctr $< 0.5\\%$.Outputs:Reason Code: STALE_HIGH_VOLUME (if stale & high volume), STALE_CONTENT (stale only), HIGH_VOLUME_DECAY (high volume only), or LOW_SIGNAL.Action Label: PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH ($\\text{Score} \\ge 75$), QUEUE_FOR_REVIEW ($50 \\le \\text{Score} < 75$), or NO_ACTION ($\\text{Score} < 50$)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Exported 30,000 ranked rows to work/outputs/baseline_action_score.csv\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_baseline_queue(df):\n",
    "    scores = []\n",
    "    reason_codes = []\n",
    "    actions = []\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for _, row in df.iterrows():\n",
    "        score = 0\n",
    "        reasons = []\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if row['days_since_last_update'] > 90:\n",
    "            score += 35\n",
    "            reasons.append('STALE')\n",
    "        elif row['days_since_last_update'] > 30:\n",
    "            score += 15\n",
    "            \n",
    "        if row['impressions_90d'] >= 3000:\n",
    "            score += 35\n",
    "            reasons.append('HIGH_VOLUME')\n",
    "        elif row['impressions_90d'] >= 1000:\n",
    "            score += 15\n",
    "            \n",
    "        if 4.0 <= row['avg_position'] <= 20.0:\n",
    "            score += 20\n",
    "            reasons.append('STRIKING_POS')\n",
    "            \n",
    "        if row['ctr'] < 0.5:\n",
    "            score += 10\n",
    "            \n",
    "        # Assign primary reason code\n",
    "        if 'STALE' in reasons and 'HIGH_VOLUME' in reasons:\n",
    "            reason_code = 'STALE_HIGH_VOLUME'\n",
    "        elif 'STALE' in reasons:\n",
    "            reason_code = 'STALE_CONTENT'\n",
    "        elif 'HIGH_VOLUME' in reasons:\n",
    "            reason_code = 'HIGH_VOLUME_DECAY'\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            reason_code = 'LOW_SIGNAL'\n",
    "            \n",
    "        # Assign action label\n",
    "        if score >= 75:\n",
    "            action = 'PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH'\n",
    "        elif score >= 50:\n",
    "            action = 'QUEUE_FOR_REVIEW'\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            action = 'NO_ACTION'\n",
    "            \n",
    "        scores.append(score)\n",
    "        reason_codes.append(reason_code)\n",
    "        actions.append(action)\n",
    "        \n",
    "    df['baseline_score'] = scores\n",
    "    df['reason_code'] = reason_codes\n",
    "    df['action_label'] = actions\n",
    "    return df\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute scores and rank\n",
    "df_scored = compute_baseline_queue(df)\n",
    "df_ranked = df_scored.sort_values(by=['baseline_score', 'impressions_90d'], ascending=[False, False]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Export CSV to work/outputs/\n",
    "os.makedirs('../outputs', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "output_cols = ['content_id', 'client_id', 'content_type', 'content_age_days', 'days_since_last_update', 'impressions_90d', 'avg_position', 'ctr', 'baseline_score', 'reason_code', 'action_label']\n",
    "df_ranked[output_cols].to_csv('../outputs/baseline_action_score.csv', index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Exported {len(df_ranked):,} ranked rows to work/outputs/baseline_action_score.csv\")"
   ]
  },
