   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f06924ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Row 1 (content_5fe46e04994d): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 517k impressions, position 4.2, not updated in 104 days. | What makes it wrong: Traffic drop may be driven by seasonal query drops rather than stale content.Row 2 (content_cb112fce36be): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 309k impressions, position 5.6, stale (104 days). | What makes it wrong: Low CTR (0.16%) could reflect informational intent where users get answers directly on SERP.Row 3 (content_36ff89c8214e): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 295k impressions, position 7.3, CTR 0.05%. | What makes it wrong: The page might rank for broad terms where click-through intent is naturally near zero.Row 4 (content_c21024970297): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 211k impressions, position 5.1, stale (104 days). | What makes it wrong: High baseline engagement rate might mean existing traffic converts well despite stale age.Row 5 (content_c8e9d6ab9013): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 208k impressions, position 9.7, 0.00% CTR. | What makes it wrong: A 0% CTR at position 9.7 indicates snippet mismatch or ranking for irrelevant impressions.Row 6 (content_d17681677e69): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 201k impressions, position 5.8, stale (104 days). | What makes it wrong: Competitor domain dominance might prevent ranking recovery even after a content refresh.Row 7 (content_a7427266c305): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 201k impressions, position 5.7, CTR 0.11%. | What makes it wrong: Editorial rewrite might accidentally remove core ranking keywords.Row 8 (content_c5063073d048): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 192k impressions, striking position 12.5. | What makes it wrong: Position 12.5 requires technical backlink support, not just text updates.Row 9 (content_3d94572c3a35): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 190k impressions, position 4.3, stale (104 days). | What makes it wrong: High impression volume could be driven by single un-monetized head terms.Row 10 (content_01908772c6db): PRIORITY_EDITORIAL_REFRESH | Why: 187k impressions, position 4.0, CTR 0.45%. | What makes it wrong: Good position and CTR suggest page is performing adequately despite 104-day staleness.Rows 11–20: All flagged under STALE_HIGH_VOLUME due to high impression scale ($>140\\text{k}$) combined with $>90$ days without updates. Weakness across group: Fixed score treats all sites identically regardless of client domain authority."
   ]
  },
